+# Perf history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+No measured p95 found in this repository (checkout at `0cb51ab`) for the
+UserPromptSubmit hook's full-recall path on an adversarial synthetic 30-word
+vocabulary, before or after a term-selection fix.
+
+Searched: `crates/muninn-core/src/recall.rs` (the read path itself, including
+its `select_terms` IDF top-8 logic and its test module), `research/00-evidence-log.md`,
+`design/ENGINE.md`, `docs/`, and the full git history of `recall.rs` reachable
+from this checkout. The only related figures on record are prototype
+benchmarks in `research/00-evidence-log.md` ([H6]: BM25 stage cost with 24 vs.
+8 IDF terms, 21.53 ms -> 4.65 ms p50 on a 50 000-record corpus) and an
+end-to-end hook measurement ([I3]: 4.07 ms p50 / 4.31 ms p95 with intent,
+0.49 ms p50 / 0.56 ms p95 without). Neither is on a 30-word adversarial
+vocabulary, and neither is described as before/after a term-selection fix.
+
+A string matching this description ("the p95 was 10.27 ms on the synthetic
+vocab", later changed to 12.34 ms) exists only as literal text inside a unit
+test assertion for `best_passage` in later commits of this repository's
+history, not in this checkout, and carries no build, dataset, or methodology
+description — it is test fixture text, not a benchmark result. It is not
+reported here.
